    <div class="publication-details">
      <h2>CodeBind: Decoupled Representation Learning for Multimodal Alignment with Unified Compositional Codebook</h2>
      <p class="publication-venue">Findings of the 64th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL 2026)</p>
      <p>Multimodal representation alignment is pivotal for large language models and robotics, but information discrepancies and scarce paired data often produce suboptimal alignment spaces. CodeBind uses a shared-and-specific compositional codebook to bridge modalities incrementally while preserving modality-unique details. Across nine modalities, it achieves state-of-the-art multimodal classification and retrieval performance.</p>
      <p class="publication-links">
        <a href="https://visual-ai.github.io/codebind" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">Project</a>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18257" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">arXiv</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Visual-AI/CodeBind" class="btn btn-sm z-depth-0" role="button">Code</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

